  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of Members States to develop fair and effective labour migration frameworks institutions and services to protect migrant workers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will support the governance of labour migration and the labour market through a range of interventions related to policies, systems, institutional capacity building and services. Certain interventions are specifically targeted to reach worker migrants, as an identified vulnerable group, while other institutions serve all workers and employers. This will include guidance on matters related to labour administration and governance. One of the expected results is the broader institutional capacity-building programme, to improve capacities and labour administration effectiveness within the various bodies to further enhance the implementation and delivery of the Ministry of Labour services. ILO will provide training, share international good practices, and provide inputs on systems and processes. This training is expected to be fully aligned or even integrated into the plans of the respective Departments in the Ministry of Labour.</narrative>
  </description>
